  {
   "id": 243498,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Photography development laboratories generally use red lighting to allow workers to see without damaging the developing photographs. Why might this be the case?\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 763393,
     "content_html": "Red light carries less damaging energy than other wavelengths of visible light."
    },
    {
     "id": 763392,
     "content_html": "Red light carries more energy than other wavelengths of visible light and can pass through without causing damage."
    },
    {
     "id": 763391,
     "content_html": "The greater frequency of red light compared with other visible light causes fewer vibrations in the developing photos."
    },
    {
     "id": 763390,
     "content_html": "The shorter wavelength of  red light compared with other visible light causes fewer vibrations in the developing photos"
    }
   ],
